window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b185-de0f2aff7ab05530.json"]={sha256:"de0f2aff7ab055300ed3332f55a3a6d21613f95f41fbf42d2f02b72a5793fcc5",value:{"id":"b185","title":"微型樁托底補強","titleEn":"Micropile underpinning","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"微型樁托底的關鍵不只是把樁打到深處，而是建立既有柱、承台、連接件與地層之間可驗證的新力流。本課逐步檢查鋼材與黏結承載、預載移交、樁群剛度、無側限段挫屈與低淨高接頭，最後用長期沉陷判讀新舊基礎是否確實共同工作。","summaryEn":"Micropile underpinning requires a verified new load path from existing columns through caps and connectors into ground. The course examines steel and bond resistance, preloaded transfer, group stiffness, buckling in unsupported zones and low-headroom joints, then interprets long-term settlement to establish interaction between old and new foundations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-ground","subcategoryTitle":"地盤改良與地下維護","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground improvement and underground maintenance","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-ground","learningTags":["underground","ug-ground","ground"],"architectureFamily":"ground","architectureNodes":[["既有荷載清冊","Existing-load inventory"],["鋼材軸應力","Steel axial stress"],["承台連接","Cap connection"],["無側限段挫屈","Unsupported-length buckling"],["低淨高接頭","Low-headroom splices"],["移交後沉陷","Post-transfer settlement"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[3,0]],"diagram":{"type":"ground","labels":["既有荷載清冊","鋼材軸應力","承台連接","無側限段挫屈","低淨高接頭"],"labelsEn":["Existing-load inventory","Steel axial stress","Cap connection","Unsupported-length buckling","Low-headroom splices"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學例：現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，在本例同時使用情境下合計1200 kN。若只增加現有柱力10%至880 kN，其他兩項維持不變，合計變成1280 kN，總需求增加80 kN或6.67%，而不是10%。還須按上部結構規範建立荷載組合，並確定新舊基礎如何分力。此加總不代表每根新樁平均分擔，也不證明承台連接或荷載移交完成；應以樁力、承台位移及現況調查共同驗證。","textEn":"Original teaching example: an existing column carries 800 kN, an extension adds 250 kN and equipment adds 150 kN, giving 1200 kN in this simultaneous-use scenario. Increase only the existing-column component by 10% to 880 kN while holding the others fixed: total demand becomes 1280 kN, up 80 kN or 6.67%, not 10%. Appropriate structural load combinations and new-old foundation sharing remain necessary. This sum implies neither equal sharing by new piles nor completed cap connection and load transfer. Verify those using pile forces, cap movement and existing-condition investigation.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b185-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證」與「鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification\" and \"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b185-v14-01","title":"既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「既有荷載清冊」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Existing-load inventory” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"托底設計須先辨識目前柱力與未來增載，不能把原設計圖的基礎反力直接當成現況。使用變更、加建及設備集中載重會改變分配，施工期間的臨時支承也需單獨列出，才能決定新樁要接管多少力與何時接管。直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「既有荷載清冊」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Underpinning starts with current column forces and future additions rather than assuming original foundation reactions still apply. Changes of use, extensions and concentrated equipment alter load distribution, and temporary support requires a separate case. These distinctions determine how much load new piles must take and when transfer occurs. Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Existing-load inventory” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，服務荷載合計P=800+250+150=1200 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For existing column force 800 kN, extension 250 kN and equipment 150 kN, combined service load P=1200 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「既有荷載清冊」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Existing-load inventory”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-01-k1","title":"既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification","text":"托底設計須先辨識目前柱力與未來增載，不能把原設計圖的基礎反力直接當成現況。使用變更、加建及設備集中載重會改變分配，施工期間的臨時支承也需單獨列出，才能決定新樁要接管多少力與何時接管。","textEn":"Underpinning starts with current column forces and future additions rather than assuming original foundation reactions still apply. Changes of use, extensions and concentrated equipment alter load distribution, and temporary support requires a separate case.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。","托底設計須先辨識目前柱力與未來增載，不能把原設計圖的基礎反力直接當成現況。","微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。"],"optionsEn":["New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant.","Underpinning starts with current column forces and future additions rather than assuming original foundation reactions still apply.","Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"托底設計須先辨識目前柱力與未來增載，不能把原設計圖的基礎反力直接當成現況。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Underpinning starts with current column forces and future additions rather than assuming original foundation reactions still apply. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b185-v14-02","title":"既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「既有荷載清冊」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Existing-load inventory” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，服務荷載合計P=800+250+150=1200 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For existing column force 800 kN, extension 250 kN and equipment 150 kN, combined service load P=1200 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對現況尺寸、使用荷載及裂縫沉陷紀錄，將不同時期荷載分列，與上部結構模型交叉核查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check existing dimensions, imposed loads and cracking-settlement records, separating load stages and cross-checking them against the superstructure model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，服務荷載合計P=800+250+150=1200 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For existing column force 800 kN, extension 250 kN and equipment 150 kN, combined service load P=1200 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。","同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","原創教學假設：假設現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，服務荷載合計P=800+250+150=1200 kN。"],"optionsEn":["A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate.","Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","Original teaching assumptions: For existing column force 800 kN, extension 250 kN and equipment 150 kN, combined service load P=1200 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設現有柱力800 kN、增建250 kN、設備150 kN，服務荷載合計P=800+250+150=1200 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For existing column force 800 kN, extension 250 kN and equipment 150 kN, combined service load P=1200 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b185-v14-03","title":"既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「既有荷載清冊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Existing-load inventory” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對現況尺寸、使用荷載及裂縫沉陷紀錄，將不同時期荷載分列，與上部結構模型交叉核查。荷載清冊應由上部結構與基礎設計者共同簽認；施工階段和最終使用階段不可混用未標示的力值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check existing dimensions, imposed loads and cracking-settlement records, separating load stages and cross-checking them against the superstructure model. Superstructure and foundation designers jointly sign the load inventory; construction and final-use forces must not be mixed without explicit stage labels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：荷載清冊應由上部結構與基礎設計者共同簽認；施工階段和最終使用階段不可混用未標示的力值。直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Superstructure and foundation designers jointly sign the load inventory; construction and final-use forces must not be mixed without explicit stage labels. Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition.","failure":"注意干擾：漏列新增設備或移除原支承，會使微型樁承擔超出假設的荷載，造成移交後持續沉陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted equipment loads or removed original support can impose more load than assumed, causing continued settlement after transfer. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對現況尺寸、使用荷載及裂縫沉陷紀錄，將不同時期荷載分列，與上部結構模型交叉核查。荷載清冊應由上部結構與基礎設計者共同簽認；施工階段和最終使用階段不可混用未標示的力值。","textEn":"Check existing dimensions, imposed loads and cracking-settlement records, separating load stages and cross-checking them against the superstructure model. Superstructure and foundation designers jointly sign the load inventory; construction and final-use forces must not be mixed without explicit stage labels.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"荷載清冊應由上部結構與基礎設計者共同簽認；施工階段和最終使用階段不可混用未標示的力值。直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。","textEn":"Superstructure and foundation designers jointly sign the load inventory; construction and final-use forces must not be mixed without explicit stage labels. Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對現況尺寸、使用荷載及裂縫沉陷紀錄，將不同時期荷載分列，與上部結構模型交叉核查。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Check existing dimensions, imposed loads and cracking-settlement records, separating load stages and cross-checking them against the superstructure model.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對現況尺寸、使用荷載及裂縫沉陷紀錄，將不同時期荷載分列，與上部結構模型交叉核查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check existing dimensions, imposed loads and cracking-settlement records, separating load stages and cross-checking them against the superstructure model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b185-v14-04","title":"既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「既有荷載清冊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Existing-load inventory” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏列新增設備或移除原支承，會使微型樁承擔超出假設的荷載，造成移交後持續沉陷。直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted equipment loads or removed original support can impose more load than assumed, causing continued settlement after transfer. Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏列新增設備或移除原支承，會使微型樁承擔超出假設的荷載，造成移交後持續沉陷。直接相加只描述本例同時服務荷載，沒有套用設計分項係數；不同作用組合及既有基礎可分擔比例需另行建立。","textEn":"Omitted equipment loads or removed original support can impose more load than assumed, causing continued settlement after transfer. Direct addition describes simultaneous service loads in this example only; design factors, combinations and the share retained by existing foundations require separate definition.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「既有荷載清冊的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Existing-load inventory mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","漏列新增設備或移除原支承，會使微型樁承擔超出假設的荷載，造成移交後持續沉陷。","微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitted equipment loads or removed original support can impose more load than assumed, causing continued settlement after transfer.","Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏列新增設備或移除原支承，會使微型樁承擔超出假設的荷載，造成移交後持續沉陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted equipment loads or removed original support can impose more load than assumed, causing continued settlement after transfer. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b185-v14-05","title":"鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「鋼材軸應力」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel axial stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"微型樁的鋼套管或鋼筋與水泥漿共同傳遞軸力，鋼材分擔比例取決於剛度及接頭連續性。先把全部力分配給鋼材可作特定保守假設，但不代表漿體永遠不參與；腐蝕餘量、套管接頭與局部挫屈也不能靠平均應力取代。這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼材軸應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Steel casing or bars share axial force with grout according to stiffness and continuity. Assigning all force to steel may be a specified conservative assumption, but does not imply grout never participates. Corrosion allowance, casing joints and local buckling also require checks beyond an average axial stress. This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Steel axial stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設鋼材獨自承受P=600 kN、有效鋼面積As=0.004 m²，σs=P/As=150 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: If steel alone carries P=600 kN over effective area As=0.004 m², σs=P/As=150 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼材軸應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Steel axial stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-05-k1","title":"鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification","text":"微型樁的鋼套管或鋼筋與水泥漿共同傳遞軸力，鋼材分擔比例取決於剛度及接頭連續性。先把全部力分配給鋼材可作特定保守假設，但不代表漿體永遠不參與；腐蝕餘量、套管接頭與局部挫屈也不能靠平均應力取代。","textEn":"Steel casing or bars share axial force with grout according to stiffness and continuity. Assigning all force to steel may be a specified conservative assumption, but does not imply grout never participates.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。","注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。","微型樁的鋼套管或鋼筋與水泥漿共同傳遞軸力，鋼材分擔比例取決於剛度及接頭連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks.","High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.","Steel casing or bars share axial force with grout according to stiffness and continuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"微型樁的鋼套管或鋼筋與水泥漿共同傳遞軸力，鋼材分擔比例取決於剛度及接頭連續性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Steel casing or bars share axial force with grout according to stiffness and continuity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b185-v14-06","title":"鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼材軸應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel axial stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設鋼材獨自承受P=600 kN、有效鋼面積As=0.004 m²，σs=P/As=150 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: If steel alone carries P=600 kN over effective area As=0.004 m², σs=P/As=150 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對鋼材證書、實際壁厚與接頭型式，將載重試驗應變比較鋼漿共同作用假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify steel certificates, actual thickness and connection type, comparing load-test strains with the assumed steel-grout composite action.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設鋼材獨自承受P=600 kN、有效鋼面積As=0.004 m²，σs=P/As=150 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: If steel alone carries P=600 kN over effective area As=0.004 m², σs=P/As=150 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設鋼材獨自承受P=600 kN、有效鋼面積As=0.004 m²，σs=P/As=150 MPa。","新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。","微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: If steel alone carries P=600 kN over effective area As=0.004 m², σs=P/As=150 MPa.","Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally.","A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設鋼材獨自承受P=600 kN、有效鋼面積As=0.004 m²，σs=P/As=150 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: If steel alone carries P=600 kN over effective area As=0.004 m², σs=P/As=150 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b185-v14-07","title":"鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼材軸應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel axial stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對鋼材證書、實際壁厚與接頭型式，將載重試驗應變比較鋼漿共同作用假設。竣工資料需保留鋼材批號、套管長度及接頭位置；結構設計者確認有效截面後才能接受材料替代。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify steel certificates, actual thickness and connection type, comparing load-test strains with the assumed steel-grout composite action. Retain steel batches, casing lengths and joint positions; the structural designer confirms effective sections before accepting material substitutions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：竣工資料需保留鋼材批號、套管長度及接頭位置；結構設計者確認有效截面後才能接受材料替代。這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain steel batches, casing lengths and joint positions; the structural designer confirms effective sections before accepting material substitutions. This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path.","failure":"注意干擾：把名目壁厚當有效面積可能忽略腐蝕或螺紋減弱，接頭也可能先於完整鋼管失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using nominal thickness can ignore corrosion or thread reductions, and connections may fail before an intact casing section. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對鋼材證書、實際壁厚與接頭型式，將載重試驗應變比較鋼漿共同作用假設。竣工資料需保留鋼材批號、套管長度及接頭位置；結構設計者確認有效截面後才能接受材料替代。","textEn":"Verify steel certificates, actual thickness and connection type, comparing load-test strains with the assumed steel-grout composite action. Retain steel batches, casing lengths and joint positions; the structural designer confirms effective sections before accepting material substitutions.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"竣工資料需保留鋼材批號、套管長度及接頭位置；結構設計者確認有效截面後才能接受材料替代。這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。","textEn":"Retain steel batches, casing lengths and joint positions; the structural designer confirms effective sections before accepting material substitutions. This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對鋼材證書、實際壁厚與接頭型式，將載重試驗應變比較鋼漿共同作用假設。","接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Verify steel certificates, actual thickness and connection type, comparing load-test strains with the assumed steel-grout composite action.","More splices affect speed only and never structural quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對鋼材證書、實際壁厚與接頭型式，將載重試驗應變比較鋼漿共同作用假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify steel certificates, actual thickness and connection type, comparing load-test strains with the assumed steel-grout composite action. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b185-v14-08","title":"鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼材軸應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel axial stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把名目壁厚當有效面積可能忽略腐蝕或螺紋減弱，接頭也可能先於完整鋼管失效。這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using nominal thickness can ignore corrosion or thread reductions, and connections may fail before an intact casing section. This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把名目壁厚當有效面積可能忽略腐蝕或螺紋減弱，接頭也可能先於完整鋼管失效。這是指定分力下的平均應力，不是微型樁整體承載力；鋼材、漿體、連接及地層黏結需依相容荷載路徑分別檢查。","textEn":"Using nominal thickness can ignore corrosion or thread reductions, and connections may fail before an intact casing section. This is mean stress under an assigned force, not total micropile capacity; steel, grout, connections and ground bond require separate checks on a compatible load path.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼材軸應力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Steel axial stress mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。","把名目壁厚當有效面積可能忽略腐蝕或螺紋減弱，接頭也可能先於完整鋼管失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.","Using nominal thickness can ignore corrosion or thread reductions, and connections may fail before an intact casing section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把名目壁厚當有效面積可能忽略腐蝕或螺紋減弱，接頭也可能先於完整鋼管失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using nominal thickness can ignore corrosion or thread reductions, and connections may fail before an intact casing section. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b185-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「地層黏結承載的機理與驗證」與「承台連接的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification\" and \"Cap connection mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b185-v14-09","title":"地層黏結承載的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「地層黏結承載」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ground-bond resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"樁端進入良好地層後，軸力沿漿土界面的剪力逐步傳出，荷載傳遞不一定均勻。注漿方式與地層條件影響有效直徑及黏結能力，不能把灌入量直接換成可靠樁徑；承載驗證需要代表性試驗及鑽孔紀錄共同支持。本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地層黏結承載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Axial force transfers progressively through grout-ground shear in the competent stratum and is not necessarily uniform along the bond. Grouting and ground conditions affect effective diameter and bond resistance, but injected volume does not directly establish a reliable diameter. Representative testing and bore records jointly support resistance assessment. The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ground-bond resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設D=0.2 m、黏結長L=8 m、平均可用剪應力τ=150 kPa，R=πDLτ=754 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For D=0.2 m, bond length L=8 m and assumed usable mean shear τ=150 kPa, R=πDLτ=754 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地層黏結承載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ground-bond resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-09-k1","title":"地層黏結承載的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification","text":"樁端進入良好地層後，軸力沿漿土界面的剪力逐步傳出，荷載傳遞不一定均勻。注漿方式與地層條件影響有效直徑及黏結能力，不能把灌入量直接換成可靠樁徑；承載驗證需要代表性試驗及鑽孔紀錄共同支持。","textEn":"Axial force transfers progressively through grout-ground shear in the competent stratum and is not necessarily uniform along the bond. Grouting and ground conditions affect effective diameter and bond resistance, but injected volume does not directly establish a reliable diameter.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地層黏結承載的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["樁端進入良好地層後，軸力沿漿土界面的剪力逐步傳出，荷載傳遞不一定均勻。","注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。","微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。"],"optionsEn":["Axial force transfers progressively through grout-ground shear in the competent stratum and is not necessarily uniform along the bond.","High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.","A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"樁端進入良好地層後，軸力沿漿土界面的剪力逐步傳出，荷載傳遞不一定均勻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Axial force transfers progressively through grout-ground shear in the competent stratum and is not necessarily uniform along the bond. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b185-v14-10","title":"地層黏結承載的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地層黏結承載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ground-bond resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設D=0.2 m、黏結長L=8 m、平均可用剪應力τ=150 kPa，R=πDLτ=754 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For D=0.2 m, bond length L=8 m and assumed usable mean shear τ=150 kPa, R=πDLτ=754 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將鑽孔地層、注漿回流及試驗曲線按樁號連結，檢查錨固層是否連續並比較不同樁的移動趨勢。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Link bore geology, grout returns and load-test curves by pile identifier, checking continuity of the bond stratum and comparing movement trends between piles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設D=0.2 m、黏結長L=8 m、平均可用剪應力τ=150 kPa，R=πDLτ=754 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For D=0.2 m, bond length L=8 m and assumed usable mean shear τ=150 kPa, R=πDLτ=754 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地層黏結承載的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","原創教學假設：假設D=0.2 m、黏結長L=8 m、平均可用剪應力τ=150 kPa，R=πDLτ=754 kN。","柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","Original teaching assumptions: For D=0.2 m, bond length L=8 m and assumed usable mean shear τ=150 kPa, R=πDLτ=754 kN.","A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設D=0.2 m、黏結長L=8 m、平均可用剪應力τ=150 kPa，R=πDLτ=754 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For D=0.2 m, bond length L=8 m and assumed usable mean shear τ=150 kPa, R=πDLτ=754 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b185-v14-11","title":"地層黏結承載的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地層黏結承載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ground-bond resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將鑽孔地層、注漿回流及試驗曲線按樁號連結，檢查錨固層是否連續並比較不同樁的移動趨勢。黏結參數及驗證樁位置需由地工設計者核准；任何異常回流或地層變更都要保留追查紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Link bore geology, grout returns and load-test curves by pile identifier, checking continuity of the bond stratum and comparing movement trends between piles. The geotechnical designer approves bond parameters and verification-pile locations; abnormal returns or changed strata retain traceable investigation records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：黏結參數及驗證樁位置需由地工設計者核准；任何異常回流或地層變更都要保留追查紀錄。本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。","observationEn":"Site practice: The geotechnical designer approves bond parameters and verification-pile locations; abnormal returns or changed strata retain traceable investigation records. The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep.","failure":"注意干擾：黏結段跨入軟弱夾層或漿體不連續會使力集中，可能出現漸進滑移而非鋼材先降伏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Weak interbeds or discontinuous grout concentrate transfer and can produce progressive slip before steel yielding. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將鑽孔地層、注漿回流及試驗曲線按樁號連結，檢查錨固層是否連續並比較不同樁的移動趨勢。黏結參數及驗證樁位置需由地工設計者核准；任何異常回流或地層變更都要保留追查紀錄。","textEn":"Link bore geology, grout returns and load-test curves by pile identifier, checking continuity of the bond stratum and comparing movement trends between piles. The geotechnical designer approves bond parameters and verification-pile locations; abnormal returns or changed strata retain traceable investigation records.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"黏結參數及驗證樁位置需由地工設計者核准；任何異常回流或地層變更都要保留追查紀錄。本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。","textEn":"The geotechnical designer approves bond parameters and verification-pile locations; abnormal returns or changed strata retain traceable investigation records. The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地層黏結承載的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。","將鑽孔地層、注漿回流及試驗曲線按樁號連結，檢查錨固層是否連續並比較不同樁的移動趨勢。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring.","Link bore geology, grout returns and load-test curves by pile identifier, checking continuity of the bond stratum and comparing movement trends between piles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將鑽孔地層、注漿回流及試驗曲線按樁號連結，檢查錨固層是否連續並比較不同樁的移動趨勢。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Link bore geology, grout returns and load-test curves by pile identifier, checking continuity of the bond stratum and comparing movement trends between piles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b185-v14-12","title":"地層黏結承載的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地層黏結承載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ground-bond resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"黏結段跨入軟弱夾層或漿體不連續會使力集中，可能出現漸進滑移而非鋼材先降伏。本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Weak interbeds or discontinuous grout concentrate transfer and can produce progressive slip before steel yielding. The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"黏結段跨入軟弱夾層或漿體不連續會使力集中，可能出現漸進滑移而非鋼材先降伏。本式假設均勻平均剪力且有效直徑可信，未含群體作用與長期效應；試驗允收還需同時檢查位移和潛變。","textEn":"Weak interbeds or discontinuous grout concentrate transfer and can produce progressive slip before steel yielding. The expression assumes uniform mean shear and credible diameter, excluding group and long-term effects; test acceptance must also address displacement and creep.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地層黏結承載的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ground-bond resistance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["黏結段跨入軟弱夾層或漿體不連續會使力集中，可能出現漸進滑移而非鋼材先降伏。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。"],"optionsEn":["Weak interbeds or discontinuous grout concentrate transfer and can produce progressive slip before steel yielding.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"黏結段跨入軟弱夾層或漿體不連續會使力集中，可能出現漸進滑移而非鋼材先降伏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Weak interbeds or discontinuous grout concentrate transfer and can produce progressive slip before steel yielding. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b185-v14-13","title":"承台連接的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cap connection mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「承台連接」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cap connection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新微型樁必須透過承台、剪力環或其他核定連接把力接入舊基礎，單樁有容量不等於既有柱力已找到新路徑。舊混凝土品質、邊距及鋼筋位置會控制局部承壓與劈裂，施工擾動也可能削弱原有基礎的剩餘能力。平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「承台連接」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New micropiles need a cap, shear rings or another approved connector to receive load from the old foundation. Pile capacity alone does not establish a new path for column force. Existing concrete quality, edge distance and reinforcement govern local bearing and splitting, while construction disturbance may reduce residual foundation capacity. Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cap connection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設連接傳力P=400 kN、有效承壓面A=0.08 m²，p=P/A=5 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For transferred connection force P=400 kN and effective bearing area A=0.08 m², p=P/A=5 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「承台連接」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cap connection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-13-k1","title":"承台連接的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Cap connection mechanism and verification","text":"新微型樁必須透過承台、剪力環或其他核定連接把力接入舊基礎，單樁有容量不等於既有柱力已找到新路徑。舊混凝土品質、邊距及鋼筋位置會控制局部承壓與劈裂，施工擾動也可能削弱原有基礎的剩餘能力。","textEn":"New micropiles need a cap, shear rings or another approved connector to receive load from the old foundation. Pile capacity alone does not establish a new path for column force.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「承台連接的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cap connection mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。","新微型樁必須透過承台、剪力環或其他核定連接把力接入舊基礎，單樁有容量不等於既有柱力已找到新路徑。","新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。"],"optionsEn":["A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate.","New micropiles need a cap, shear rings or another approved connector to receive load from the old foundation.","Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新微型樁必須透過承台、剪力環或其他核定連接把力接入舊基礎，單樁有容量不等於既有柱力已找到新路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New micropiles need a cap, shear rings or another approved connector to receive load from the old foundation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b185-v14-14","title":"承台連接的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cap connection mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「承台連接」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cap connection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設連接傳力P=400 kN、有效承壓面A=0.08 m²，p=P/A=5 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For transferred connection force P=400 kN and effective bearing area A=0.08 m², p=P/A=5 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以探測及局部取樣確認舊基礎，核對連接面與鋼筋淨距，將實際傳力方向放入節點模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Investigate the existing foundation with scanning and justified sampling, verify connection faces and reinforcement clearance, and model the actual force direction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設連接傳力P=400 kN、有效承壓面A=0.08 m²，p=P/A=5 MPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For transferred connection force P=400 kN and effective bearing area A=0.08 m², p=P/A=5 MPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「承台連接的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cap connection mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。","接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。","原創教學假設：假設連接傳力P=400 kN、有效承壓面A=0.08 m²，p=P/A=5 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length.","More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.","Original teaching assumptions: For transferred connection force P=400 kN and effective bearing area A=0.08 m², p=P/A=5 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設連接傳力P=400 kN、有效承壓面A=0.08 m²，p=P/A=5 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For transferred connection force P=400 kN and effective bearing area A=0.08 m², p=P/A=5 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b185-v14-15","title":"承台連接的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cap connection mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「承台連接」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cap connection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以探測及局部取樣確認舊基礎，核對連接面與鋼筋淨距，將實際傳力方向放入節點模型。連接細部應在現況調查後核定；舊構件切削與新增孔洞由既有結構設計者確認剩餘力流再施工。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Investigate the existing foundation with scanning and justified sampling, verify connection faces and reinforcement clearance, and model the actual force direction. Finalize connections after existing-condition investigation; the existing-structure designer confirms remaining load paths before cutting or drilling new openings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：連接細部應在現況調查後核定；舊構件切削與新增孔洞由既有結構設計者確認剩餘力流再施工。平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。","observationEn":"Site practice: Finalize connections after existing-condition investigation; the existing-structure designer confirms remaining load paths before cutting or drilling new openings. Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：舊混凝土劈裂或接面滑移會使新樁未能接管，即使單樁載重試驗合格，柱仍持續下沉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Splitting of old concrete or interface slip can prevent takeover despite a successful pile load test, leaving the column settling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以探測及局部取樣確認舊基礎，核對連接面與鋼筋淨距，將實際傳力方向放入節點模型。連接細部應在現況調查後核定；舊構件切削與新增孔洞由既有結構設計者確認剩餘力流再施工。","textEn":"Investigate the existing foundation with scanning and justified sampling, verify connection faces and reinforcement clearance, and model the actual force direction. Finalize connections after existing-condition investigation; the existing-structure designer confirms remaining load paths before cutting or drilling new openings.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"連接細部應在現況調查後核定；舊構件切削與新增孔洞由既有結構設計者確認剩餘力流再施工。平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。","textEn":"Finalize connections after existing-condition investigation; the existing-structure designer confirms remaining load paths before cutting or drilling new openings. Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「承台連接的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cap connection mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以探測及局部取樣確認舊基礎，核對連接面與鋼筋淨距，將實際傳力方向放入節點模型。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。"],"optionsEn":["Investigate the existing foundation with scanning and justified sampling, verify connection faces and reinforcement clearance, and model the actual force direction.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以探測及局部取樣確認舊基礎，核對連接面與鋼筋淨距，將實際傳力方向放入節點模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Investigate the existing foundation with scanning and justified sampling, verify connection faces and reinforcement clearance, and model the actual force direction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b185-v14-16","title":"承台連接的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cap connection mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「承台連接」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cap connection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊混凝土劈裂或接面滑移會使新樁未能接管，即使單樁載重試驗合格，柱仍持續下沉。平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Splitting of old concrete or interface slip can prevent takeover despite a successful pile load test, leaving the column settling. Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊混凝土劈裂或接面滑移會使新樁未能接管，即使單樁載重試驗合格，柱仍持續下沉。平均承壓不包含局部劈裂、沖切及錨定需求，舊材料強度亦可能不均；完整節點驗算不能由此單式取代。","textEn":"Splitting of old concrete or interface slip can prevent takeover despite a successful pile load test, leaving the column settling. Mean bearing excludes splitting, punching and anchorage, and existing strength may vary; this single equation cannot replace complete node analysis.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「承台連接的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cap connection mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","舊混凝土劈裂或接面滑移會使新樁未能接管，即使單樁載重試驗合格，柱仍持續下沉。","新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Splitting of old concrete or interface slip can prevent takeover despite a successful pile load test, leaving the column settling.","Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"舊混凝土劈裂或接面滑移會使新樁未能接管，即使單樁載重試驗合格，柱仍持續下沉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Splitting of old concrete or interface slip can prevent takeover despite a successful pile load test, leaving the column settling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b185-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「預載荷載移交的機理與驗證」與「新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification\" and \"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b185-v14-17","title":"預載荷載移交的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「預載荷載移交」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Preloaded transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新樁若沒有預先接觸或預載，往往要等舊基礎再沉陷才逐步動員，不能假設施工完成即分擔設計荷載。預載的目的在控制接管路徑及位移，但過大推力也可能抬升上部結構；須同時監測力與柱、承台的相對移動。剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預載荷載移交」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Without established contact or preload, a new pile may need further old-foundation settlement before it mobilizes. Completion alone does not mean it carries the intended share. Preload controls transfer and movement, but excessive force can lift the structure, requiring simultaneous force and relative column-cap displacement monitoring. The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Preloaded transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設需移交ΔP=300 kN、等效剛度k=100 kN/mm，彈性位移δ=ΔP/k=3 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For transfer increment ΔP=300 kN and equivalent stiffness k=100 kN/mm, elastic movement δ=ΔP/k=3 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預載荷載移交」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Preloaded transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-17-k1","title":"預載荷載移交的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification","text":"新樁若沒有預先接觸或預載，往往要等舊基礎再沉陷才逐步動員，不能假設施工完成即分擔設計荷載。預載的目的在控制接管路徑及位移，但過大推力也可能抬升上部結構；須同時監測力與柱、承台的相對移動。","textEn":"Without established contact or preload, a new pile may need further old-foundation settlement before it mobilizes. Completion alone does not mean it carries the intended share.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預載荷載移交的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。","同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","新樁若沒有預先接觸或預載，往往要等舊基礎再沉陷才逐步動員，不能假設施工完成即分擔設計荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally.","Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","Without established contact or preload, a new pile may need further old-foundation settlement before it mobilizes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新樁若沒有預先接觸或預載，往往要等舊基礎再沉陷才逐步動員，不能假設施工完成即分擔設計荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Without established contact or preload, a new pile may need further old-foundation settlement before it mobilizes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b185-v14-18","title":"預載荷載移交的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預載荷載移交」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Preloaded transfer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設需移交ΔP=300 kN、等效剛度k=100 kN/mm，彈性位移δ=ΔP/k=3 mm。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For transfer increment ΔP=300 kN and equivalent stiffness k=100 kN/mm, elastic movement δ=ΔP/k=3 mm. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對新樁力、舊基礎沉陷與連接間隙，確認接管過程沒有造成局部抬升或未知支承卸載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare new-pile force, old-foundation settlement and connection gaps to confirm that transfer causes neither local uplift nor unintended unloading elsewhere.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設需移交ΔP=300 kN、等效剛度k=100 kN/mm，彈性位移δ=ΔP/k=3 mm。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For transfer increment ΔP=300 kN and equivalent stiffness k=100 kN/mm, elastic movement δ=ΔP/k=3 mm. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預載荷載移交的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設需移交ΔP=300 kN、等效剛度k=100 kN/mm，彈性位移δ=ΔP/k=3 mm。","柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。","載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For transfer increment ΔP=300 kN and equivalent stiffness k=100 kN/mm, elastic movement δ=ΔP/k=3 mm.","A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension.","Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設需移交ΔP=300 kN、等效剛度k=100 kN/mm，彈性位移δ=ΔP/k=3 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For transfer increment ΔP=300 kN and equivalent stiffness k=100 kN/mm, elastic movement δ=ΔP/k=3 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b185-v14-19","title":"預載荷載移交的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預載荷載移交」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Preloaded transfer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對新樁力、舊基礎沉陷與連接間隙，確認接管過程沒有造成局部抬升或未知支承卸載。荷載移交須設結構及地工共同停留點；核定力位移範圍後，才可解除原有臨時支承。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare new-pile force, old-foundation settlement and connection gaps to confirm that transfer causes neither local uplift nor unintended unloading elsewhere. Load transfer requires a joint structural-geotechnical hold point; original temporary support is released only after approved force-displacement conditions are demonstrated. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：荷載移交須設結構及地工共同停留點；核定力位移範圍後，才可解除原有臨時支承。剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。","observationEn":"Site practice: Load transfer requires a joint structural-geotechnical hold point; original temporary support is released only after approved force-displacement conditions are demonstrated. The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets.","failure":"注意干擾：只看施加荷重而不看位移，可能在接管前先抬升樓板，損傷既有脆性接縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Monitoring applied force without movement can lift slabs before intended transfer and damage existing brittle joints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對新樁力、舊基礎沉陷與連接間隙，確認接管過程沒有造成局部抬升或未知支承卸載。荷載移交須設結構及地工共同停留點；核定力位移範圍後，才可解除原有臨時支承。","textEn":"Compare new-pile force, old-foundation settlement and connection gaps to confirm that transfer causes neither local uplift nor unintended unloading elsewhere. Load transfer requires a joint structural-geotechnical hold point; original temporary support is released only after approved force-displacement conditions are demonstrated.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"荷載移交須設結構及地工共同停留點；核定力位移範圍後，才可解除原有臨時支承。剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。","textEn":"Load transfer requires a joint structural-geotechnical hold point; original temporary support is released only after approved force-displacement conditions are demonstrated. The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預載荷載移交的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比對新樁力、舊基礎沉陷與連接間隙，確認接管過程沒有造成局部抬升或未知支承卸載。","微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare new-pile force, old-foundation settlement and connection gaps to confirm that transfer causes neither local uplift nor unintended unloading elsewhere.","Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比對新樁力、舊基礎沉陷與連接間隙，確認接管過程沒有造成局部抬升或未知支承卸載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare new-pile force, old-foundation settlement and connection gaps to confirm that transfer causes neither local uplift nor unintended unloading elsewhere. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b185-v14-20","title":"預載荷載移交的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預載荷載移交」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Preloaded transfer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看施加荷重而不看位移，可能在接管前先抬升樓板，損傷既有脆性接縫。剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Monitoring applied force without movement can lift slabs before intended transfer and damage existing brittle joints. The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看施加荷重而不看位移，可能在接管前先抬升樓板，損傷既有脆性接縫。剛度位移式假設接觸已建立且線性，未含原始間隙與舊基礎塑性；本例不提供現場頂升程序或施力目標。","textEn":"Monitoring applied force without movement can lift slabs before intended transfer and damage existing brittle joints. The stiffness relation assumes established linear contact and excludes initial gaps and old-foundation plasticity; it does not prescribe jacking procedures or field force targets.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預載荷載移交的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Preloaded transfer mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","只看施加荷重而不看位移，可能在接管前先抬升樓板，損傷既有脆性接縫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","Monitoring applied force without movement can lift slabs before intended transfer and damage existing brittle joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看施加荷重而不看位移，可能在接管前先抬升樓板，損傷既有脆性接縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Monitoring applied force without movement can lift slabs before intended transfer and damage existing brittle joints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b185-v14-21","title":"新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「新舊樁群分力」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pile-group load sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"共用承台下不同樁的剛度與初始接觸決定荷載分配，並非單純按樁數平均。新樁與舊基礎可能有不同沉陷歷史與端承條件；等位移模型有助說明剛度比例，但需要承台近似剛性且沒有額外轉動才成立。並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「新舊樁群分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Relative stiffness and initial contact govern load sharing beneath a common cap rather than pile count alone. New piles and old foundations have different settlement histories and toe conditions. An equal-displacement model illustrates stiffness sharing only when the cap is sufficiently rigid and additional rotation is absent. Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pile-group load sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設兩組剛度k₁=200、k₂=100 MN/m，共承P=1200 kN且等位移，P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For groups k₁=200 and k₂=100 MN/m sharing P=1200 kN at equal displacement, P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「新舊樁群分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pile-group load sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-21-k1","title":"新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification","text":"共用承台下不同樁的剛度與初始接觸決定荷載分配，並非單純按樁數平均。新樁與舊基礎可能有不同沉陷歷史與端承條件；等位移模型有助說明剛度比例，但需要承台近似剛性且沒有額外轉動才成立。","textEn":"Relative stiffness and initial contact govern load sharing beneath a common cap rather than pile count alone. New piles and old foundations have different settlement histories and toe conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["共用承台下不同樁的剛度與初始接觸決定荷載分配，並非單純按樁數平均。","同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Relative stiffness and initial contact govern load sharing beneath a common cap rather than pile count alone.","Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用承台下不同樁的剛度與初始接觸決定荷載分配，並非單純按樁數平均。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Relative stiffness and initial contact govern load sharing beneath a common cap rather than pile count alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b185-v14-22","title":"新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「新舊樁群分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pile-group load sharing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設兩組剛度k₁=200、k₂=100 MN/m，共承P=1200 kN且等位移，P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For groups k₁=200 and k₂=100 MN/m sharing P=1200 kN at equal displacement, P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測承台轉角與代表樁軸力，核對是否等位移，將不同樁的載重試驗剛度用於比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure cap rotation and representative pile forces to test equal displacement, using individual load-test stiffnesses for comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設兩組剛度k₁=200、k₂=100 MN/m，共承P=1200 kN且等位移，P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For groups k₁=200 and k₂=100 MN/m sharing P=1200 kN at equal displacement, P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。","原創教學假設：假設兩組剛度k₁=200、k₂=100 MN/m，共承P=1200 kN且等位移，P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN。","新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。"],"optionsEn":["More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.","Original teaching assumptions: For groups k₁=200 and k₂=100 MN/m sharing P=1200 kN at equal displacement, P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN.","New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設兩組剛度k₁=200、k₂=100 MN/m，共承P=1200 kN且等位移，P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For groups k₁=200 and k₂=100 MN/m sharing P=1200 kN at equal displacement, P₁=Pk₁/(k₁+k₂)=800 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b185-v14-23","title":"新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「新舊樁群分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pile-group load sharing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測承台轉角與代表樁軸力，核對是否等位移，將不同樁的載重試驗剛度用於比較。分力模型應納入承台轉動與初始荷載；基礎設計者用試驗及監測修正後，再核定最終移交狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure cap rotation and representative pile forces to test equal displacement, using individual load-test stiffnesses for comparison. Include cap rotation and initial loading in sharing models; the foundation designer updates them with tests and monitoring before approving final transfer. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分力模型應納入承台轉動與初始荷載；基礎設計者用試驗及監測修正後，再核定最終移交狀態。並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Include cap rotation and initial loading in sharing models; the foundation designer updates them with tests and monitoring before approving final transfer. Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging.","failure":"注意干擾：把剛度不同的樁平均分力，可能讓較硬新樁提前超載，較軟支承卻尚未有效參與。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal-force allocation between unequal stiffnesses can overload the stiff new group before softer supports contribute effectively. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測承台轉角與代表樁軸力，核對是否等位移，將不同樁的載重試驗剛度用於比較。分力模型應納入承台轉動與初始荷載；基礎設計者用試驗及監測修正後，再核定最終移交狀態。","textEn":"Measure cap rotation and representative pile forces to test equal displacement, using individual load-test stiffnesses for comparison. Include cap rotation and initial loading in sharing models; the foundation designer updates them with tests and monitoring before approving final transfer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分力模型應納入承台轉動與初始荷載；基礎設計者用試驗及監測修正後，再核定最終移交狀態。並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。","textEn":"Include cap rotation and initial loading in sharing models; the foundation designer updates them with tests and monitoring before approving final transfer. Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。","量測承台轉角與代表樁軸力，核對是否等位移，將不同樁的載重試驗剛度用於比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.","Measure cap rotation and representative pile forces to test equal displacement, using individual load-test stiffnesses for comparison."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測承台轉角與代表樁軸力，核對是否等位移，將不同樁的載重試驗剛度用於比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure cap rotation and representative pile forces to test equal displacement, using individual load-test stiffnesses for comparison. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b185-v14-24","title":"新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「新舊樁群分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pile-group load sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把剛度不同的樁平均分力，可能讓較硬新樁提前超載，較軟支承卻尚未有效參與。並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal-force allocation between unequal stiffnesses can overload the stiff new group before softer supports contribute effectively. Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把剛度不同的樁平均分力，可能讓較硬新樁提前超載，較軟支承卻尚未有效參與。並聯彈簧模型未含土體群效與非線性，單組剛度應對應相同荷載區間；舊樁歷史力不能直接重新平均。","textEn":"Equal-force allocation between unequal stiffnesses can overload the stiff new group before softer supports contribute effectively. Parallel springs exclude group-soil interaction and nonlinearity; stiffnesses must correspond to the same load range, and historical force in old piles cannot simply be redistributed by averaging.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「新舊樁群分力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pile-group load sharing mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把剛度不同的樁平均分力，可能讓較硬新樁提前超載，較軟支承卻尚未有效參與。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Equal-force allocation between unequal stiffnesses can overload the stiff new group before softer supports contribute effectively.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把剛度不同的樁平均分力，可能讓較硬新樁提前超載，較軟支承卻尚未有效參與。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal-force allocation between unequal stiffnesses can overload the stiff new group before softer supports contribute effectively. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b185-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證」與「偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification\" and \"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b185-v14-25","title":"無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「無側限段挫屈」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unsupported-length buckling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"微型樁通常受到周圍地層側向約束，但穿越空洞、極軟層或施工開挖區時可能形成無側限長度。鋼套管的挫屈能力便成為重要限制，不能因樁很深就假設全長都有連續支承；接頭偏心與腐蝕也會放大不利影響。歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「無側限段挫屈」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ground normally restrains micropiles laterally, but voids, very soft layers or excavation can create unsupported lengths. Casing buckling then becomes critical; depth does not guarantee continuous support. Joint eccentricity and corrosion amplify the vulnerability and require checking the actual restrained length rather than assuming full confinement. Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unsupported-length buckling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：理想鉸接段L=4 m、E=200 GPa、I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴，Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For an ideal pinned unsupported segment L=4 m, E=200 GPa and I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴, Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「無側限段挫屈」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unsupported-length buckling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-25-k1","title":"無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification","text":"微型樁通常受到周圍地層側向約束，但穿越空洞、極軟層或施工開挖區時可能形成無側限長度。鋼套管的挫屈能力便成為重要限制，不能因樁很深就假設全長都有連續支承；接頭偏心與腐蝕也會放大不利影響。","textEn":"Ground normally restrains micropiles laterally, but voids, very soft layers or excavation can create unsupported lengths. Casing buckling then becomes critical; depth does not guarantee continuous support.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。","微型樁通常受到周圍地層側向約束，但穿越空洞、極軟層或施工開挖區時可能形成無側限長度。","柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。"],"optionsEn":["A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length.","Ground normally restrains micropiles laterally, but voids, very soft layers or excavation can create unsupported lengths.","A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"微型樁通常受到周圍地層側向約束，但穿越空洞、極軟層或施工開挖區時可能形成無側限長度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ground normally restrains micropiles laterally, but voids, very soft layers or excavation can create unsupported lengths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b185-v14-26","title":"無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「無側限段挫屈」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unsupported-length buckling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：理想鉸接段L=4 m、E=200 GPa、I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴，Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For an ideal pinned unsupported segment L=4 m, E=200 GPa and I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴, Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依鑽孔與開挖紀錄界定無側限區，核對套管接頭位置與直線度，檢查橫向地層彈簧可信度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define unsupported zones from drilling and excavation records, check casing-joint locations and straightness, and assess credibility of lateral ground springs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：理想鉸接段L=4 m、E=200 GPa、I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴，Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For an ideal pinned unsupported segment L=4 m, E=200 GPa and I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴, Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。","微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。","原創教學假設：理想鉸接段L=4 m、E=200 GPa、I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴，Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring.","Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks.","Original teaching assumptions: For an ideal pinned unsupported segment L=4 m, E=200 GPa and I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴, Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：理想鉸接段L=4 m、E=200 GPa、I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴，Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For an ideal pinned unsupported segment L=4 m, E=200 GPa and I=1×10⁻⁵ m⁴, Pcr=π²EI/L²=1.23 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b185-v14-27","title":"無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「無側限段挫屈」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unsupported-length buckling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依鑽孔與開挖紀錄界定無側限區，核對套管接頭位置與直線度，檢查橫向地層彈簧可信度。無側限區與套管需求應明列於施工圖；地層流失或新增開挖發現後，設計者須重新核對穩定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define unsupported zones from drilling and excavation records, check casing-joint locations and straightness, and assess credibility of lateral ground springs. Show unsupported zones and casing requirements on drawings; the designer reassesses stability when ground loss or additional excavation occurs. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：無側限區與套管需求應明列於施工圖；地層流失或新增開挖發現後，設計者須重新核對穩定。歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。","observationEn":"Site practice: Show unsupported zones and casing requirements on drawings; the designer reassesses stability when ground loss or additional excavation occurs. Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint.","failure":"注意干擾：隱藏空洞使有效長度增加，可能在軸應力仍低時發生挫屈，造成托底支承突然失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A hidden void increases effective length and may trigger buckling at low axial stress, abruptly compromising underpinning support. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依鑽孔與開挖紀錄界定無側限區，核對套管接頭位置與直線度，檢查橫向地層彈簧可信度。無側限區與套管需求應明列於施工圖；地層流失或新增開挖發現後，設計者須重新核對穩定。","textEn":"Define unsupported zones from drilling and excavation records, check casing-joint locations and straightness, and assess credibility of lateral ground springs. Show unsupported zones and casing requirements on drawings; the designer reassesses stability when ground loss or additional excavation occurs.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"無側限區與套管需求應明列於施工圖；地層流失或新增開挖發現後，設計者須重新核對穩定。歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。","textEn":"Show unsupported zones and casing requirements on drawings; the designer reassesses stability when ground loss or additional excavation occurs. Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification\"?","options":["依鑽孔與開挖紀錄界定無側限區，核對套管接頭位置與直線度，檢查橫向地層彈簧可信度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。"],"optionsEn":["Define unsupported zones from drilling and excavation records, check casing-joint locations and straightness, and assess credibility of lateral ground springs.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依鑽孔與開挖紀錄界定無側限區，核對套管接頭位置與直線度，檢查橫向地層彈簧可信度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define unsupported zones from drilling and excavation records, check casing-joint locations and straightness, and assess credibility of lateral ground springs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b185-v14-28","title":"無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「無側限段挫屈」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unsupported-length buckling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"隱藏空洞使有效長度增加，可能在軸應力仍低時發生挫屈，造成托底支承突然失效。歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A hidden void increases effective length and may trigger buckling at low axial stress, abruptly compromising underpinning support. Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"隱藏空洞使有效長度增加，可能在軸應力仍低時發生挫屈，造成托底支承突然失效。歐拉荷重是理想彈性上限，不是允許工作荷載；實際承載需考慮初彎、接頭、塑性與有效端部拘束。","textEn":"A hidden void increases effective length and may trigger buckling at low axial stress, abruptly compromising underpinning support. Euler load is an ideal elastic limit, not working-load permission; actual resistance includes bow, joints, plasticity and effective end restraint.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「無側限段挫屈的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unsupported-length buckling mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","隱藏空洞使有效長度增加，可能在軸應力仍低時發生挫屈，造成托底支承突然失效。","柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A hidden void increases effective length and may trigger buckling at low axial stress, abruptly compromising underpinning support.","A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隱藏空洞使有效長度增加，可能在軸應力仍低時發生挫屈，造成托底支承突然失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A hidden void increases effective length and may trigger buckling at low axial stress, abruptly compromising underpinning support. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b185-v14-29","title":"偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「偏心樁群反力」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eccentric group reactions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"柱中心與新樁群中心不一致時，除了總軸力還會產生力矩，承台需透過不同樁反力或拉壓偶抵抗。若只把總力平均分到樁上，邊樁需求會被低估；既有基礎是否仍接觸也會改變可用的反力分布。力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偏心樁群反力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An offset between column and new pile-group centres creates moment in addition to total axial load. The cap resists it through unequal reactions or a tension-compression couple. Averaging total force underestimates edge-pile demand, while continued contact with the original foundation changes the available reaction distribution. The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eccentric group reactions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設需抵抗力矩M=300 kN·m、兩反力線距s=2 m，力偶增量ΔP=M/s=150 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For moment M=300 kN·m and reaction-line spacing s=2 m, couple-force increment ΔP=M/s=150 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偏心樁群反力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eccentric group reactions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-29-k1","title":"偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification","text":"柱中心與新樁群中心不一致時，除了總軸力還會產生力矩，承台需透過不同樁反力或拉壓偶抵抗。若只把總力平均分到樁上，邊樁需求會被低估；既有基礎是否仍接觸也會改變可用的反力分布。","textEn":"An offset between column and new pile-group centres creates moment in addition to total axial load. The cap resists it through unequal reactions or a tension-compression couple.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。","接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。","柱中心與新樁群中心不一致時，除了總軸力還會產生力矩，承台需透過不同樁反力或拉壓偶抵抗。"],"optionsEn":["A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension.","More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.","An offset between column and new pile-group centres creates moment in addition to total axial load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"柱中心與新樁群中心不一致時，除了總軸力還會產生力矩，承台需透過不同樁反力或拉壓偶抵抗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An offset between column and new pile-group centres creates moment in addition to total axial load. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b185-v14-30","title":"偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偏心樁群反力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eccentric group reactions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設需抵抗力矩M=300 kN·m、兩反力線距s=2 m，力偶增量ΔP=M/s=150 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For moment M=300 kN·m and reaction-line spacing s=2 m, couple-force increment ΔP=M/s=150 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對柱樁中心與實際樁位，量測承台轉角及邊樁力，將接觸或離縫狀態納入模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check actual column and pile centres, measure cap rotation and edge forces, and include contact or separation in the model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設需抵抗力矩M=300 kN·m、兩反力線距s=2 m，力偶增量ΔP=M/s=150 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For moment M=300 kN·m and reaction-line spacing s=2 m, couple-force increment ΔP=M/s=150 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設需抵抗力矩M=300 kN·m、兩反力線距s=2 m，力偶增量ΔP=M/s=150 kN。","新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。","注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For moment M=300 kN·m and reaction-line spacing s=2 m, couple-force increment ΔP=M/s=150 kN.","New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant.","High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設需抵抗力矩M=300 kN·m、兩反力線距s=2 m，力偶增量ΔP=M/s=150 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For moment M=300 kN·m and reaction-line spacing s=2 m, couple-force increment ΔP=M/s=150 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b185-v14-31","title":"偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偏心樁群反力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eccentric group reactions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對柱樁中心與實際樁位，量測承台轉角及邊樁力，將接觸或離縫狀態納入模型。群樁設計應列垂直力及雙向彎矩組合；樁位超差須由基礎設計者核准重新分力後才驗收。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check actual column and pile centres, measure cap rotation and edge forces, and include contact or separation in the model. Group design includes vertical force and biaxial moment combinations; the foundation designer redistributes forces and approves out-of-position piles before acceptance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：群樁設計應列垂直力及雙向彎矩組合；樁位超差須由基礎設計者核准重新分力後才驗收。力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Group design includes vertical force and biaxial moment combinations; the foundation designer redistributes forces and approves out-of-position piles before acceptance. The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer.","failure":"注意干擾：邊樁可能受拉而原設計只查受壓，接頭與舊承台因此可能先裂開，形成非預期荷載重分配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An edge pile may enter tension although only compression was checked, cracking connections or the old cap and redistributing load unexpectedly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對柱樁中心與實際樁位，量測承台轉角及邊樁力，將接觸或離縫狀態納入模型。群樁設計應列垂直力及雙向彎矩組合；樁位超差須由基礎設計者核准重新分力後才驗收。","textEn":"Check actual column and pile centres, measure cap rotation and edge forces, and include contact or separation in the model. Group design includes vertical force and biaxial moment combinations; the foundation designer redistributes forces and approves out-of-position piles before acceptance.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"群樁設計應列垂直力及雙向彎矩組合；樁位超差須由基礎設計者核准重新分力後才驗收。力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。","textEn":"Group design includes vertical force and biaxial moment combinations; the foundation designer redistributes forces and approves out-of-position piles before acceptance. The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對柱樁中心與實際樁位，量測承台轉角及邊樁力，將接觸或離縫狀態納入模型。","新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check actual column and pile centres, measure cap rotation and edge forces, and include contact or separation in the model.","Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對柱樁中心與實際樁位，量測承台轉角及邊樁力，將接觸或離縫狀態納入模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check actual column and pile centres, measure cap rotation and edge forces, and include contact or separation in the model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b185-v14-32","title":"偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偏心樁群反力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eccentric group reactions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"邊樁可能受拉而原設計只查受壓，接頭與舊承台因此可能先裂開，形成非預期荷載重分配。力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An edge pile may enter tension although only compression was checked, cracking connections or the old cap and redistributing load unexpectedly. The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「柱力是向下的，就不可能讓任何托底樁受到拉力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A downward column load can never put an underpinning pile in tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"邊樁可能受拉而原設計只查受壓，接頭與舊承台因此可能先裂開，形成非預期荷載重分配。力偶式只給兩反力線的增量，不是每樁總力；須加上平均軸力並檢查承台剛度及拉力傳遞是否成立。","textEn":"An edge pile may enter tension although only compression was checked, cracking connections or the old cap and redistributing load unexpectedly. The couple equation gives the increment on two reaction lines, not total force per pile; add mean axial load and verify cap stiffness and tensile transfer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偏心樁群反力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eccentric group reactions mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。","邊樁可能受拉而原設計只查受壓，接頭與舊承台因此可能先裂開，形成非預期荷載重分配。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.","An edge pile may enter tension although only compression was checked, cracking connections or the old cap and redistributing load unexpectedly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊樁可能受拉而原設計只查受壓，接頭與舊承台因此可能先裂開，形成非預期荷載重分配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An edge pile may enter tension although only compression was checked, cracking connections or the old cap and redistributing load unexpectedly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b185-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「低淨高接頭的機理與驗證」與「移交後沉陷的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification\" and \"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b185-v14-33","title":"低淨高接頭的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「低淨高接頭」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low-headroom splices” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"受限空間的微型樁需以短節鋼材連接，接頭數增加就增加製造、安裝與檢查界面。每個接頭必須傳遞設計軸力及可能的彎曲，螺紋有效截面與套管同軸度也影響承載；施工方便不能取代接合性能證明。節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低淨高接頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Restricted headroom requires short steel sections, increasing fabrication, installation and inspection interfaces. Every splice must transfer design axial force and possible bending, while thread-root area and casing alignment affect resistance. Ease of installation cannot substitute for evidence that the connection performs under the required force combinations. The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-headroom splices” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設總長L=18 m、每節有效長l=1.5 m，需n=ceil(L/l)=12節，通常有11個節間接頭。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For total length L=18 m and effective section length l=1.5 m, n=ceil(L/l)=12 sections, normally with eleven inter-section joints.","failure":"常見誤解：「接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低淨高接頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low-headroom splices”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-33-k1","title":"低淨高接頭的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification","text":"受限空間的微型樁需以短節鋼材連接，接頭數增加就增加製造、安裝與檢查界面。每個接頭必須傳遞設計軸力及可能的彎曲，螺紋有效截面與套管同軸度也影響承載；施工方便不能取代接合性能證明。","textEn":"Restricted headroom requires short steel sections, increasing fabrication, installation and inspection interfaces. Every splice must transfer design axial force and possible bending, while thread-root area and casing alignment affect resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More splices affect speed only and never structural quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低淨高接頭的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["受限空間的微型樁需以短節鋼材連接，接頭數增加就增加製造、安裝與檢查界面。","接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。","載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。"],"optionsEn":["Restricted headroom requires short steel sections, increasing fabrication, installation and inspection interfaces.","More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.","Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受限空間的微型樁需以短節鋼材連接，接頭數增加就增加製造、安裝與檢查界面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Restricted headroom requires short steel sections, increasing fabrication, installation and inspection interfaces. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b185-v14-34","title":"低淨高接頭的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低淨高接頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low-headroom splices” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設總長L=18 m、每節有效長l=1.5 m，需n=ceil(L/l)=12節，通常有11個節間接頭。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For total length L=18 m and effective section length l=1.5 m, n=ceil(L/l)=12 sections, normally with eleven inter-section joints. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每節長度、接頭序號與安裝證據，對照實際接頭深度及高彎曲或腐蝕區，查漏裝與錯件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify section lengths, splice identifiers and installation evidence against actual depths and high-bending or corrosion zones, checking missing or mismatched parts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設總長L=18 m、每節有效長l=1.5 m，需n=ceil(L/l)=12節，通常有11個節間接頭。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For total length L=18 m and effective section length l=1.5 m, n=ceil(L/l)=12 sections, normally with eleven inter-section joints. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低淨高接頭的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["微型樁平均鋼應力不高，就不用檢查接頭與局部挫屈。","原創教學假設：假設總長L=18 m、每節有效長l=1.5 m，需n=ceil(L/l)=12節，通常有11個節間接頭。","微型樁試驗合格就代表與舊基礎的連接也合格。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean steel stress removes the need for connection and local-buckling checks.","Original teaching assumptions: For total length L=18 m and effective section length l=1.5 m, n=ceil(L/l)=12 sections, normally with eleven inter-section joints.","A successful micropile load test proves the old-foundation connection is adequate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設總長L=18 m、每節有效長l=1.5 m，需n=ceil(L/l)=12節，通常有11個節間接頭。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For total length L=18 m and effective section length l=1.5 m, n=ceil(L/l)=12 sections, normally with eleven inter-section joints. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b185-v14-35","title":"低淨高接頭的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低淨高接頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low-headroom splices” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每節長度、接頭序號與安裝證據，對照實際接頭深度及高彎曲或腐蝕區，查漏裝與錯件。接頭型式、檢驗方法及追溯編碼須由結構設計者核准；未完成接合檢查的鋼節不得以後續注漿取代驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify section lengths, splice identifiers and installation evidence against actual depths and high-bending or corrosion zones, checking missing or mismatched parts. The structural designer approves splice type, inspection and traceability; later grouting cannot replace verification of an unaccepted steel connection. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：接頭型式、檢驗方法及追溯編碼須由結構設計者核准；未完成接合檢查的鋼節不得以後續注漿取代驗證。節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural designer approves splice type, inspection and traceability; later grouting cannot replace verification of an unaccepted steel connection. The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭未完全接合或軸線偏移會降低有效容量，深埋後難以直接檢查，可能成為長期薄弱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incomplete engagement or misalignment reduces effective resistance and can become a long-term weak point that is difficult to inspect after burial. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每節長度、接頭序號與安裝證據，對照實際接頭深度及高彎曲或腐蝕區，查漏裝與錯件。接頭型式、檢驗方法及追溯編碼須由結構設計者核准；未完成接合檢查的鋼節不得以後續注漿取代驗證。","textEn":"Verify section lengths, splice identifiers and installation evidence against actual depths and high-bending or corrosion zones, checking missing or mismatched parts. The structural designer approves splice type, inspection and traceability; later grouting cannot replace verification of an unaccepted steel connection.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"接頭型式、檢驗方法及追溯編碼須由結構設計者核准；未完成接合檢查的鋼節不得以後續注漿取代驗證。節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。","textEn":"The structural designer approves splice type, inspection and traceability; later grouting cannot replace verification of an unaccepted steel connection. The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低淨高接頭的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","同一承台下所有微型樁一定平均分擔柱力。","核對每節長度、接頭序號與安裝證據，對照實際接頭深度及高彎曲或腐蝕區，查漏裝與錯件。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every micropile under one cap necessarily shares column load equally.","Verify section lengths, splice identifiers and installation evidence against actual depths and high-bending or corrosion zones, checking missing or mismatched parts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對每節長度、接頭序號與安裝證據，對照實際接頭深度及高彎曲或腐蝕區，查漏裝與錯件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify section lengths, splice identifiers and installation evidence against actual depths and high-bending or corrosion zones, checking missing or mismatched parts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b185-v14-36","title":"低淨高接頭的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低淨高接頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low-headroom splices” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭未完全接合或軸線偏移會降低有效容量，深埋後難以直接檢查，可能成為長期薄弱點。節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incomplete engagement or misalignment reduces effective resistance and can become a long-term weak point that is difficult to inspect after burial. The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接頭越多只會影響速度，不會影響樁的受力品質。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More splices affect speed only and never structural quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭未完全接合或軸線偏移會降低有效容量，深埋後難以直接檢查，可能成為長期薄弱點。節數計算假設有效長度已扣除接合損失，並非加工切割清單；實際端部、接頭搭接與設備淨高需另外協調。","textEn":"Incomplete engagement or misalignment reduces effective resistance and can become a long-term weak point that is difficult to inspect after burial. The section count assumes effective lengths already exclude connection loss and is not a fabrication cut list; ends, overlap and equipment headroom require separate coordination.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低淨高接頭的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low-headroom splices mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["接頭未完全接合或軸線偏移會降低有效容量，深埋後難以直接檢查，可能成為長期薄弱點。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。"],"optionsEn":["Incomplete engagement or misalignment reduces effective resistance and can become a long-term weak point that is difficult to inspect after burial.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭未完全接合或軸線偏移會降低有效容量，深埋後難以直接檢查，可能成為長期薄弱點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incomplete engagement or misalignment reduces effective resistance and can become a long-term weak point that is difficult to inspect after burial. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b185-v14-37","title":"移交後沉陷的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「移交後沉陷」如何影響微型樁托底補強的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-transfer settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Micropile underpinning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"托底後的沉陷可能來自新樁動員、舊土層壓密或連接變形，不應只以短期試驗合格結束觀察。長期趨勢需與荷載使用、地下水及季節變化一起判讀，固定基準與測點位置則是區分真變形與量測漂移的前提。平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「移交後沉陷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Post-underpinning settlement may reflect new-pile mobilization, consolidation of old soils or connection movement, so short-term test acceptance should not end observation. Long-term trends require load-use, groundwater and seasonal context, with stable references and fixed measurement locations to distinguish actual deformation from instrumental drift. The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post-transfer settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設沉陷由3 mm增至4 mm、間隔6 month，平均速率v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For settlement increasing from 3 mm to 4 mm over six months, mean rate v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month.","failure":"常見誤解：「載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「移交後沉陷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post-transfer settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-37-k1","title":"移交後沉陷的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification","text":"托底後的沉陷可能來自新樁動員、舊土層壓密或連接變形，不應只以短期試驗合格結束觀察。長期趨勢需與荷載使用、地下水及季節變化一起判讀，固定基準與測點位置則是區分真變形與量測漂移的前提。","textEn":"Post-underpinning settlement may reflect new-pile mobilization, consolidation of old soils or connection movement, so short-term test acceptance should not end observation. Long-term trends require load-use, groundwater and seasonal context, with stable references and fixed measurement locations to distinguish actual deformation from instrumental drift.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「移交後沉陷的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。","托底後的沉陷可能來自新樁動員、舊土層壓密或連接變形，不應只以短期試驗合格結束觀察。","新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。"],"optionsEn":["Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring.","Post-underpinning settlement may reflect new-pile mobilization, consolidation of old soils or connection movement, so short-term test acceptance should not end observation.","New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"托底後的沉陷可能來自新樁動員、舊土層壓密或連接變形，不應只以短期試驗合格結束觀察。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Post-underpinning settlement may reflect new-pile mobilization, consolidation of old soils or connection movement, so short-term test acceptance should not end observation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b185-v14-38","title":"移交後沉陷的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「移交後沉陷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-transfer settlement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設沉陷由3 mm增至4 mm、間隔6 month，平均速率v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For settlement increasing from 3 mm to 4 mm over six months, mean rate v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將柱、承台及相鄰未托底基礎同步水準測量，對照使用荷載及水位，檢查差異而非只看單點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Level columns, caps and adjacent untreated foundations together, comparing loads and groundwater and examining differences rather than one isolated point.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設沉陷由3 mm增至4 mm、間隔6 month，平均速率v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For settlement increasing from 3 mm to 4 mm over six months, mean rate v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「移交後沉陷的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["注漿量很多就必然得到較大且完整的黏結直徑。","新樁完工後會立刻自然承擔所有設計荷載比例。","原創教學假設：假設沉陷由3 mm增至4 mm、間隔6 month，平均速率v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month。"],"optionsEn":["High grout volume necessarily creates a larger continuous bond diameter.","Completed new piles immediately carry every intended design load share naturally.","Original teaching assumptions: For settlement increasing from 3 mm to 4 mm over six months, mean rate v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設沉陷由3 mm增至4 mm、間隔6 month，平均速率v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For settlement increasing from 3 mm to 4 mm over six months, mean rate v=(4−3)/6=0.167 mm/month. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b185-v14-39","title":"移交後沉陷的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「移交後沉陷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-transfer settlement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將柱、承台及相鄰未托底基礎同步水準測量，對照使用荷載及水位，檢查差異而非只看單點。交接列出監測期限、終止條件及使用變更通報；異常速率由地工與既有結構設計者共同判讀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Level columns, caps and adjacent untreated foundations together, comparing loads and groundwater and examining differences rather than one isolated point. Handover defines monitoring duration, closure criteria and change-of-use reporting; geotechnical and existing-structure designers jointly interpret abnormal movement rates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接列出監測期限、終止條件及使用變更通報；異常速率由地工與既有結構設計者共同判讀。平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover defines monitoring duration, closure criteria and change-of-use reporting; geotechnical and existing-structure designers jointly interpret abnormal movement rates. The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution.","failure":"注意干擾：停止追蹤可能漏掉連接逐步滑移，直到門窗卡住或新裂縫出現才發現托底尚未穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stopping observations can miss progressive connection slip until doors bind or new cracks reveal that underpinning performance has not stabilized. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將柱、承台及相鄰未托底基礎同步水準測量，對照使用荷載及水位，檢查差異而非只看單點。交接列出監測期限、終止條件及使用變更通報；異常速率由地工與既有結構設計者共同判讀。","textEn":"Level columns, caps and adjacent untreated foundations together, comparing loads and groundwater and examining differences rather than one isolated point. Handover defines monitoring duration, closure criteria and change-of-use reporting; geotechnical and existing-structure designers jointly interpret abnormal movement rates.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接列出監測期限、終止條件及使用變更通報；異常速率由地工與既有結構設計者共同判讀。平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。","textEn":"Handover defines monitoring duration, closure criteria and change-of-use reporting; geotechnical and existing-structure designers jointly interpret abnormal movement rates. The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「移交後沉陷的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將柱、承台及相鄰未托底基礎同步水準測量，對照使用荷載及水位，檢查差異而非只看單點。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","微型樁埋在地下，所以任何位置都不需要挫屈檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Level columns, caps and adjacent untreated foundations together, comparing loads and groundwater and examining differences rather than one isolated point.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A buried micropile never requires buckling checks anywhere along its length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將柱、承台及相鄰未托底基礎同步水準測量，對照使用荷載及水位，檢查差異而非只看單點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Level columns, caps and adjacent untreated foundations together, comparing loads and groundwater and examining differences rather than one isolated point. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b185-v14-40","title":"移交後沉陷的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"prerequisiteIds":["b185-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「移交後沉陷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-transfer settlement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"停止追蹤可能漏掉連接逐步滑移，直到門窗卡住或新裂縫出現才發現托底尚未穩定。平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stopping observations can miss progressive connection slip until doors bind or new cracks reveal that underpinning performance has not stabilized. The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「載重試驗通過後，既有建物不需要再做沉陷監測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing a load test removes the need for further building-settlement monitoring.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b185-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"停止追蹤可能漏掉連接逐步滑移，直到門窗卡住或新裂縫出現才發現托底尚未穩定。平均速率可能掩蓋階段性加速，且本數值不是通用合格值；應以資產容許差異變形及量測解析度制定判據。","textEn":"Stopping observations can miss progressive connection slip until doors bind or new cracks reveal that underpinning performance has not stabilized. The mean rate can conceal episodic acceleration and is not a universal acceptance value; criteria depend on tolerable differential movement and measurement resolution.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]},{"id":"b185-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「移交後沉陷的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-transfer settlement mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","停止追蹤可能漏掉連接逐步滑移，直到門窗卡住或新裂縫出現才發現托底尚未穩定。","新樁容量只要大於原設計柱力，就不用查目前用途。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Stopping observations can miss progressive connection slip until doors bind or new cracks reveal that underpinning performance has not stabilized.","New-pile capacity above the original column force makes current use irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"停止追蹤可能漏掉連接逐步滑移，直到門窗卡住或新裂縫出現才發現托底尚未穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stopping observations can miss progressive connection slip until doors bind or new cracks reveal that underpinning performance has not stabilized. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-fhwa-micro","v14s-keller-micro","v14s-geo","v14s-keller-harley","v14s-keller-gallery"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
